-- Demo machine: the writer drafts, then recreates, in turn. Out of turn (a second draft before a
-- recreate, or a recreate first) is refused, and any other Notion write, which
-- examples/demo/draft.yaml translates to `other`, is denied. complier doesn't observe Notion, so
-- nothing here waits on the world. FDR proves and compiles this at `complier machine up`.
datatype Role = writer
datatype Act = draft | recreate | other
Policy = Draft
Draft = Permit(writer, draft, Recreate) [] Deny(writer, other, Draft)
Recreate = Permit(writer, recreate, Draft) [] Deny(writer, other, Recreate)
